<title>UK: Macfarlane sees flat A$ trend with good inflation.</title>
<headline>Macfarlane sees flat A$ trend with good inflation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) governor Ian Macfarlane said on Thursday the trend for Australia's currency would remain flat as long as inflation was respectable.</p>
<p>&quot;The trend will remain flat as long as Australia continues to maintain an internationally respectable inflation outlook,&quot; Macfarlane said at a banking seminar here.</p>
<p>He said that as a free floating currency the Australian dollar was subject to fluctuations, notably because the economy was prone to quite large movements in terms of trade.</p>
<p>The Australian dollar at 1645 GMT was at US$0.7605/10.</p>
<p>-- Jacqueline Thorpe, London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
